rota lap 4917, row 2 -- Fire, the row that sees; read the threshold page and looked hard at the line every standing guard calls sound
think Lane item 1 waits on a green public seam, so I graded my whole shelf first. Nothing below B except one yonder page at 74. The shelf reads healthy, so the crux was not a grade.
think Read the REDS ledger, as the row's fixed seat asks. %702 is a front-door prose red and its instance stands repaired -- door_setting_undeclared=0, prose_register verdict=ok. Its paper's tail carried a guard proposed and not built, scoped to docs-geode, and that was the crux in my own room.
think MEASURED BEFORE BUILDING. A naive first reading -- resolve every backticked relative path against the page's directory -- refused `./bootstrap.sh` in docs-geode/tutorials/the-first-hour.md. That is a false positive and it is the interesting one: two lines above, the page says `cd rye`, and rye/bootstrap.sh exists. A bare backticked path states no base, so a reading that resolves one must guess.
think A LINK states one. Markdown resolves a relative target against the document, so both halves of a link are page-relative by the format's own rule. That single fact is the whole difference between the elder proposal and a wall: the disagreement is legible with no guess about intent, and no filesystem question about what the reader meant.
think Checked absence with the fetched scan (both instrument names absent here and upstream), opened claim petrichor-link-text-promise, pushed it, THEN built. commits_behind was 2 at the check, so the pull mattered.
obs THE CLASS IS REAL AND UNREAD. 226 living Markdown links print a backticked path their own target contradicts; 3 in docs-geode, 223 across 68 other living pages, 104 more in dated testimony. Three near neighbours each pass it correctly -- tracked_link resolves TARGETS and every target here resolves, law_tool_citation is bounded to .claude/rules/ by its own header, docs_command_path passes an absent printed path free on purpose.
obs TWO READERS, TWO PROMISES. One clicks and arrives; one copies what is shown and is sent nowhere. The line reports sound either way, which is what kept it invisible.
obs WALL WHERE I OWN THE ROOM, RATCHET WHERE I DO NOT. docs-geode gates at zero -- three repaired on this lap, so the wall refuses only what arrives after it. The 223 belong to other lanes, and a gate that reds on somebody else's work is a gate somebody turns off.
obs I DID NOT SETTLE THE CAUSE. dated_path_repoint rewrites every occurrence on a line, anchor text included, and its regex wants a dated basename most of these texts lack -- so the fold repointer is not the cause it first resembles. Named in the paper as unsettled rather than guessed at.
obs THE PEN CAUGHT TWO OF MY OWN TEST CASES. A page one directory deep makes `../room/file` correct, so my planted wrong depth resolved and the leg read no. The clamp at the tree root does the same to a doubled `..`. Both plants moved two directories deep, where the wrongness is real.
